6. ELIMINATED-INTERMEDIATE TRACKING MECHANISM (for the Todo 17 traffic report)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Chosen mechanism: two DISCARDABLE ATTRIBUTES attached to every fused op the pass
creates (set via Operation::setAttr in the rewrite pattern):
  - polykernel.fused_from      = "rmsnorm_matmul"   (StringAttr; the fusion kind)
  - polykernel.eliminated_type = <tensor type>       (TypeAttr; the eliminated
                                    rmsnorm result's tensor type/shape, e.g.
                                    tensor<1x2048x4096xbf16>)
Why attributes (not a pass statistic):
  - EXACT under the greedy driver: one tag per committed fusion. A statistic
    counter incremented inside a RewritePattern could miscount under the greedy
    driver's speculative apply/retry/rollback loop; the IR attribute cannot.
  - IR-OBSERVABLE + FileCheck-able: the lit test asserts the tags directly.
  - Zero plumbing: no pattern<->pass counter wiring; survives IR round-trip.
How Todo 17 uses it: walk the module for ops carrying `polykernel.fused_from`,
group by its value, read `polykernel.eliminated_type`, and compute the saved
global-memory round-trip per fusion as
    saved_bytes = numElements(eliminated_type) * sizeof(element_type)
(e.g. tensor<1x2048x4096xbf16> -> 1*2048*4096 elements * 2 bytes = 16 MiB saved
per inference step for the @unfused example). Sum across fused ops for the report.

