9. RISKS / NOTES FOR TODO 13 (the other fusion passes)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. PATTERN TEMPLATE: this pass is the reference. Each Todo 13 pass = an
   OpRewritePattern on the CONSUMER op, inspecting its producer(s), guarded by
   hasOneUse() on every consumed intermediate, replaceOpWithNewOp<FusedOp>(...)
   with the .td-exact operand order + carried attrs + the consumer's result type,
   eraseOp(dead producer), run under applyPatternsGreedily. Mirror the file layout
   (Passes.td def + <Name>.h + <Name>.cpp + CMake source line + Passes.h include).
2. MULTI-PRODUCER FUSIONS (e.g. fused_matmul_bias_gelu = matmul+bias+gelu,
   fused_residual_rmsnorm = add+rmsnorm): every intermediate that gets absorbed
   needs its OWN single-use check, and the chain must be matched in one pattern
   (greedy driver applies one pattern per match). Watch operand order carefully —
   fused_residual_rmsnorm is (residual, input, epsilon?), qkv_projection needs the
   num_heads attr carried.
3. MULTI-RESULT FUSIONS (qkv_projection -> Q,K,V; fused_kv_append_attention ->
   output,updated_cache): replaceOpWithNewOp must pass ALL result types; the
   single-use check applies to each consumed value, and erasing the producer(s)
   must not remove a value still used elsewhere.
4. TRACKING ATTRS: reuse the SAME two attr names (polykernel.fused_from with a
   per-fusion value like "matmul_bias_gelu", and polykernel.eliminated_type). For
   fusions eliminating MULTIPLE intermediates, either attach multiple
   eliminated-type attrs (e.g. polykernel.eliminated_type_0/_1) or an array attr —
   decide consistently so Todo 17's walker stays simple. The attribute mechanism
   (not statistics) should be kept for the exactness reason in section 6.
5. ATTR-PRINT ORDER: discardable attrs print sorted by name; epsilon (a declared
   property) sorts among them. Lit CHECK lines for fused ops should either pin the
   full dict literally (proves presence/absence precisely) or use ordered
   CHECK-SAME chains — and operand regexes must be non-greedy/non-whitespace
   (%{{[^[:space:]]*}}) so a trailing %{{.*}} does not swallow the attr dict.
6. EPSILON FLOAT FORMAT: f32 attrs reprint as the rounded value (1.0e-5 ->
   9.99999974E-6). Lit checks should use `epsilon = {{.*}} : f32`, not a pinned
   literal, unless pinning the whole dict.
